<title>CANADA: Trimac to buy Atlantic bulk trucking ops.</title>
<headline>Trimac to buy Atlantic bulk trucking ops.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trimac Corp said on Monday its wholly owned subsidiary, Trimac Transportation Services Inc, negotiated the purchase of the Atlantic Canada-based bulk trucking operations of Corporation Provost Ltee.</p>
<p>Financial details of the deal were not disclosed.</p>
<p>The purchase consists of the business and assets of Coastal Bulk Transport Ltd, Brunswick Bulk Transport Ltd, Quinnsway Transport Ltd and Brunswick Bulk USA, Trimac said.</p>
<p>The deal is expected to close this week.</p>
</text>
